Description: Disconnect the date menu's weather section from its weather client when the section is destroyed.
 WeatherSection connects to the changed signal of its WeatherClient with connect() and never disconnects. The client
 outlives the section and emits changed after a weather update, a change of location, and when the Weather app is
 installed or removed, so an emission after the shell destroyed its actors at shutdown, in the nested main loop of
 the time limits manager, runs WeatherSection._sync() on the destroyed section, and GJS logs "has been already
 disposed" criticals. The handler is connected with connectObject() now, as disconnect-app-signals-on-destroy.patch
 does for the handlers of installed-changed.
Author: Mitar
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-11-06

--- a/js/ui/dateMenu.js
+++ b/js/ui/dateMenu.js
@@ -584,7 +584,7 @@
         layout.hookup_style(this._forecastGrid);
         box.add_child(this._forecastGrid);
 
-        this._weatherClient.connect('changed', this._sync.bind(this));
+        this._weatherClient.connectObject('changed', () => this._sync(), this);
         this._sync();
     }
 
